                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e2c99f1-585a-4ef8-bd92-3f78389badea",
                                "sense_id": "725c3e43-f06b-363f-8c3b-5e8a97b37faa",
                                "text": "Yet foꝛaſmuch as it muſt of neceſſitie be knowne, what is vertue, & vice: beꝛore a mā can well, & wiſely liue, embꝛacing the one, and eſchewing the other: eyther to make ſoūde the ſicke minde (incaſe it be miſeaſed, & hath a will to bee relieued) take this doctrine, as a medicine: oꝛels to cōfirme the holle: that is to mean: incaſe you haue been well, & honeſtly trayned vp: moꝛe perfitely to perceiue the path of good maners: wherin you may walk with entire delite, and cōme to & honour of a laudable life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e0cab909-0f2f-4ce3-9970-1b25c579af04",
                                "sense_id": "725c3e43-f06b-363f-8c3b-5e8a97b37faa",
                                "text": "Upon which miſericoꝛde followeth pite, in perfoꝛming and fulfilling of charitable woꝛkes of mercie, helping & comfoꝛting him that is miseased."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b5067f3-3d0e-48a7-b6df-098f7ce03280",
                                "sense_id": "725c3e43-f06b-363f-8c3b-5e8a97b37faa",
                                "text": "Poore people and Subjectes, both miseased, & scandalized."
